          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "When connecting multi-tier enterprise systems—such as **MYOB Acumatica** (formerly MYOB Advanced), **SAP**, **CRM platforms** (Salesforce, Dynamics 365, or HubSpot), and **Microsoft 365**—you will generally look at a combination of Hobart-based enterprise IT integrators and accredited national ERP partners with dedicated Tasmanian footprints.\n\nThe most capable specialists serving the Hobart and broader Tasmanian market fall into several key categories:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Hobart-Based Enterprise Systems & Microsoft Integrators\n\n* **Intuit Technologies**\n  * **Headquarters:** Hobart (with statewide and national presence).\n  * **Core Strengths:** As one of Tasmania’s largest ICT and managed solutions firms, Intuit specializes heavily in the **Microsoft ecosystem** (Microsoft 365, Azure, Power Platform, Dynamics 365 CRM/ERP).\n  * **Best For:** Acting as the primary integration partner connecting core productivity, identity, and CRM systems (Microsoft 365 / Dynamics) into backend ERPs via Azure Integration Services and custom APIs.\n* **Datacom (Hobart Office)**\n  * **Footprint:** Major office and delivery teams in Hobart.\n  * **Core Strengths:** Datacom is a top-tier enterprise systems integrator across Australia and New Zealand. They hold deep enterprise accreditations in both **SAP** (including S/4HANA migrations and integration) and **Microsoft** (M365, Power Platform, Azure).\n  * **Best For:** High-complexity enterprise architectures, legacy ERP-to-cloud integrations, and large-scale SAP implementations needing to communicate with mid-market tools and Microsoft 365.\n* **Tempus Innovative Solutions**\n  * **Footprint:** Offices in Hobart and Melbourne.\n  * **Core Strengths:** Focuses specifically on mid-tier system integrations, custom workflows, and automation linking CRM, ERP, finance systems, and Microsoft 365/SharePoint for mid-market and association clients.\n\n---\n\n### 2. MYOB Acumatica Specialists Operating in Tasmania\n\nBecause MYOB Acumatica is delivered strictly through authorized partner channels, engaging a certified enterprise partner is required to orchestrate endpoints and REST APIs for the platform:\n\n* **BusinessHub**\n  * **Footprint:** Direct operational presence and client base in Hobart/Tasmania.\n  * **Core Strengths:** Award-winning **Platinum MYOB Acumatica Partner**. They specialize in mid-market manufacturing, wholesale distribution, and multi-entity configurations. They have deep experience integrating Acumatica’s open APIs with third-party CRMs and Microsoft environments.\n* **Stratus Consulting Group / Kilimanjaro Consulting**\n  * **Footprint:** National Diamond Partners with extensive Tasmanian project histories (e.g., Stratus implemented MYOB Acumatica for St John Ambulance Tasmania).\n  * **Core Strengths:** The largest dedicated MYOB enterprise implementers in ANZ. They specialize in complex workflows, add-ons, and integrating Acumatica with specialized operational tools, external CRMs, and finance workflows.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Cross-ERP Specialists (SAP + MYOB Acumatica)\n\n* **Leverage Technologies**\n  * **Reach:** Delivers across Tasmania and regional Australia.\n  * **Core Strengths:** Uniquely accredited in **both SAP (SAP Business One) and MYOB Acumatica**, alongside Sage.\n  * **Best For:** Situations where you run a hybrid environment (e.g., a corporate parent on SAP and a regional branch on MYOB Acumatica, or transitioning from one to the other) and need unified data consolidation, custom middleware, and CRM sync.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Selection Framework\n\n1. **If the project is centered around Microsoft 365, Azure, and CRM workflows:**\n   * Engage **Intuit Technologies** or **Datacom** to architect the middleware (using **Azure Logic Apps** or **Power Automate**) and manage data flow between your CRM and back-office apps.\n2. **If the primary challenge is MYOB Acumatica configuration and API connectivity:**\n   * Engage a dedicated Acumatica partner like **BusinessHub** (local Tasmanian focus) or **Stratus Group** to build the bidirectional sync pipelines and handle data schemas.\n3. **If connecting SAP to mid-tier applications:**\n   * Work with **Datacom** or **Leverage Technologies**, as SAP's integration layer (SAP BTP or Business One Service Layer) requires specialized certified knowledge.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
